# EcoTrack — Project Agent Rules

## Stack (do not change without explicit request)
- Framework: Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript (`src/app`)
- UI: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui (Radix). Prefer existing UI primitives over custom CSS.
- State: Zustand (`src/lib/store.ts`) with persist for entries
- NLP: `src/app/api/parse/route.ts` — OpenAI when `OPENAI_API_KEY` is set, else heuristic fallback
- Tests: Jest + React Testing Library (`npm test`)
- Folder layout:
  - `src/app` routes and API
  - `src/components` UI
  - `src/lib` store, parsers, emission factors
  - `src/hooks` client hooks
  - `src/types` shared types
  - `src/utils` helpers

## Vibe / development
- Do not narrate every line of code. Ship working features.
- On errors: propose a concrete fix immediately and apply it.
- Functionality over perfection. Keep modules small and reusable.
- Mobile-first, accessible (labels, contrast, keyboard).
- Soft micro-interactions (CSS transitions / Tailwind animate). Lazy-load heavy UI.
- Spanish UI copy (product is ES-first); keep code and comments in English.

## Product
EcoTrack MVP: log carbon footprint from natural language. Parse activity → kg CO2e → dashboard + history.

## Deploy (Replit)
- App must start with `npm run dev` / `npm start` using `.replit`.
- Never commit secrets. Use `.env.example` + Replit Secrets.
- `scripts/deploy.sh` prepares env and production build.
